{"title":"Career Roadmap: Smart Contract Tester","role":"Smart Contract Tester","summary":"A Smart Contract Tester validates blockchain smart contracts for functional correctness, security vulnerabilities, gas efficiency and expected behaviour before deployment.","facts":{"Current degree":"BCA","Course":"Blockchain / Web3"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build expertise in smart-contract testing, blockchain fundamentals, security analysis and automated testing"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Smart Contract Tester validates blockchain smart contracts for functional correctness, security vulnerabilities, gas efficiency and expected behaviour before deployment."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Blockchain fundamentals"},{"text":"Solidity"},{"text":"Software testing"},{"text":"Smart-contract security"},{"text":"Ethereum/EVM concepts"},{"text":"Automated testing"},{"text":"Code review"},{"text":"Static analysis"},{"text":"Fuzzing"},{"text":"Debugging"},{"text":"Basic cryptography"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong candidate should understand both how a smart contract is supposed to work and how it can fail or be exploited."},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Smart-contract testing is security-sensitive. Testing should be performed only on contracts, testnets or environments where the tester has authorization."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Skill","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Programming + web fundamentals"},{"text":"JavaScript, Python, Git, databases"},{"text":"Coding projects"},{"text":"Starting Solidity without programming fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Blockchain + Solidity"},{"text":"Ethereum, EVM, Solidity"},{"text":"Smart-contract projects"},{"text":"Treating blockchain as only cryptocurrency"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Smart-contract testing"},{"text":"Foundry/Hardhat, testing, security patterns"},{"text":"Automated test suites"},{"text":"Only performing manual testing"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Security testing + auditing"},{"text":"Fuzzing, static analysis, exploit analysis"},{"text":"Audit reports + capstone"},{"text":"No understanding of vulnerabilities or attack surfaces"}]]}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semester 1"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Programming fundamentals"},{"text":"Python or JavaScript"},{"text":"Data structures"},{"text":"Git/GitHub"},{"text":"Linux basics"},{"text":"Computer networks"},{"text":"Basic databases"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 2"},{"type":"p","text":"Strengthen:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"JavaScript/TypeScript"},{"text":"Object-oriented programming"},{"text":"Algorithms"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Web development"},{"text":"HTTP/API fundamentals"},{"text":"Cryptography basics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 3"},{"type":"p","text":"Start blockchain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Blockchain architecture"},{"text":"Distributed ledgers"},{"text":"Blocks"},{"text":"Transactions"},{"text":"Hashing"},{"text":"Digital signatures"},{"text":"Public/private keys"},{"text":"Wallets"},{"text":"Consensus concepts"},{"text":"Ethereum fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 4"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn Ethereum/EVM:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ethereum Virtual Machine"},{"text":"Accounts"},{"text":"Transactions"},{"text":"Gas"},{"text":"Opcodes"},{"text":"Storage"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Calldata"},{"text":"Events"},{"text":"Logs"},{"text":"ABI"},{"text":"RPC"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Start Solidity."},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 5"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Solidity syntax"},{"text":"Contracts"},{"text":"Functions"},{"tex