{"type":"p","text":"Generate many unexpected inputs to discover edge cases."},{"type":"h","text":"Invariant Testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Define conditions that must always remain true."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unauthorized users cannot withdraw funds."},{"text":"Total token supply remains consistent."},{"text":"Only authorized roles can change critical parameters."}]}]},{"heading":"Testing Tools","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Foundry"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Forge"},{"text":"Anvil"},{"text":"Cast"},{"text":"Solidity-based tests"},{"text":"Fuzzing"},{"text":"Invariant testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Hardhat"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Local blockchain"},{"text":"Contract compilation"},{"text":"Testing"},{"text":"Deployment"},{"text":"Debugging"},{"text":"Plugins"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other Tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Remix"},{"text":"Ganache-style local environments where relevant"},{"text":"OpenZeppelin Contracts"},{"text":"Ethers.js"},{"text":"viem"},{"text":"Web3.js concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a modern security-focused path, Foundry should be a major tool to learn."}]},{"heading":"Smart Contract Security","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study common vulnerability classes."},{"type":"h","text":"Reentrancy"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"External calls"},{"text":"State updates"},{"text":"Reentrant execution"},{"text":"Checks-effects-interactions"},{"text":"Reentrancy guards"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Access Control"},{"type":"p","text":"Test:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Owner functions"},{"text":"Admin functions"},{"text":"Role permissions"},{"text":"Privilege escalation"},{"text":"Missing authorization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Arithmetic & Precision"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Overflow/underflow"},{"text":"Integer division"},{"text":"Rounding"},{"text":"Decimal mismatches"},{"text":"Precision loss"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Oracle Manipulation"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Price feeds"},{"text":"Stale data"},{"text":"Incorrect validation"},{"text":"Manipulated market prices"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Signature Security"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital signatures"},{"text":"Nonces"},{"text":"Replay attacks"},{"text":"Domain separation"},{"text":"EIP-712 concepts"}]}]},{"heading":"Other Important Vulnerability Areas","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to investigate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Denial of service"},{"text":"Front-running"},{"text":"Transaction-order dependence"},{"text":"MEV"},{"text":"Flash-loan attack surfaces"},{"text":"Unchecked external calls"},{"text":"Unsafe delegate calls"},{"text":"Improper initialization"},{"text":"Upgradeability vulnerabilities"},{"text":"Proxy storage collisions"},{"text":"Logic errors"},{"text":"Insecure randomness"},{"text":"Timestamp dependence"},{"text":"Oracle failures"},{"text":"Token-standard incompatibilities"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Not every finding is exploitable in every contract; learn to distinguish theoretical weaknesses from practical attack paths."}]},{"heading":"Token Standards","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand common standards such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ERC-20"},{"text":"ERC-721"},{"text":"ERC-1155"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Token transfers"},{"text":"Approvals"},{"text":"Allowances"},{"text":"Minting"},{"text":"Burning"},{"text":"Ownership"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Transfer hooks"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Test edge cases such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Incorrect allowance handling"},{"text":"Unauthorized minting"},{"text":"Transfer restrictions"},{"text":"Reentrancy"},{"text":"Access-control errors"}]}]},{"heading":"DeFi Testing","ki